  "swing": {
    "method": "Per pair, y = p¹ − p⁰ (seat), a = P¹ − P⁰ (region), b = a·p⁰/P⁰; λ̂ = Σ(y − a)(b − a) / Σ(b − a)²; u = (y − a − λ̂(b − a)) / s(p̂); σ_seat = 1.4826 × MAD(u). σ_λ = RMS of the per-pair λ̂; σ_seat pooled over every pair's u. p̂ = max(0, p⁰ + a + λ̂(b − a)) renormalised over the seat's parties, as the engine projects; a cell with p̂ = 0, or with s(p̂) = 0 or no finite centring ratio, is left out of u.",
    "centring_method": "The engine draws a raw N(0, (σ_seat·s(p̂))²) per party and centres it with weights p̂ normalised, so a party keeps only a fraction of its raw SD (monte_carlo.centring_sd_ratio), worked out per seat × party at the seat's predicted shares. Each u is divided by its own ratio before the same robust spread, per pair and pooled: σ_seat raw = 1.4826 × MAD(u ÷ ratio).",
